      "text": "Since the mean of the set is 4, the sum of the three numbers is \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\). Let the three numbers be \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\), with \\(x = 1\\), \\(y < 4\\), and \\(z = 4\\). The median of the set is 4, so \\(y = 4\\). Now we need to find the range, which is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers. Therefore, the range is \\(z - x = 4 - 1 = 3\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).\nTo find the range of the set of numbers, we start by identifying the given information and the relationships between the numbers. We know the following:\n\n1. The set consists of three numbers: \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\).\n2. The mean of the set is 4.\n3. The median of the set is 4.\n4. The smallest number in the set is 1.\n5. The largest number in the set is 4.\n\nFrom the mean and median, we can determine the sum of the three numbers:\n\\[\nx + y + z = 12\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\(x\\) and \\(z\\):\n\\[\n1 + y + 4 = 12\n\\]\nSimplifying the equation:\n\\[\n5 + y = 12\n\\]\nSubtracting 5 from both sides:\n\\[\ny = 7\n\\]\nSo, the set of numbers is \\(1, 7, 4\\). The median is the middle number, which is 7, and since it is equal to the mean, 4, we have confirmed the values. The range of the set is the difference between the largest and smallest numbers:\n\\[\nz - x = 4 - 1 = 3\n\\]\nThus, the range of the set of numbers is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
